    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Since the sample sizes for the two marker genotypes are now $ n_{M_i M_i} = n/4 $, the sampling variance of the marker contrasts is doubled (with $ E(SE_I^2) = 8\\sigma_e^2/n $), giving the expected value of the squared marker contrast as",
      "source_page": 518,
      "printed_page": 498,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter16:p014:b10"
      ],
