      "content_sha256": "db46f3b6eaec7c6d38ab05b2aaf9a67597a261e291a14995f44e0cb711fd1f1a"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "As in the case of half-sib analysis, nested ANOVA is often used in place of sums of squared marker constrasts. The ANOVA model for full-sib families becomes",
      "source_page": 519,
      "printed_page": 499,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter16:p015:b2"
      ],
      "bbox": [
