          532.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "e56571b739fe0e1dff11b6343ed756734898b7558a3e5a04c51480844d038c0a"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "If one ignores the marker heterozygotes in intercross families and considers the marker contrasts for all informative parents, then using the same logic that leads to Equation 16.15 shows that the contribution to $ MS_m $ is $ (n/4)MC^2 $ for each informative contrast in a backcross or fully informative family and $ (n/8)MC_I^2 $ for an intercross marker contrast. Recalling Equations 16.22 and 16.23, the expected value of $ MS_m $ becomes",
      "source_page": 519,
      "printed_page": 499,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter16:p015:b5"
      ],
      "bbox": [
